.env
*.local
golang/bin/
# A build left beside the source. `go build` with no -o writes the binary next to
# the package, and one of those reached the first commit at golang/reconcile:
# 18 MB of ELF in a repository judged by people who read source.
golang/reconcile
golang/app
golang/rehearse
golang/cover/
typescript/web/node_modules/
typescript/web/dist/
# The build's server half: the same page rendered to HTML files, thrown away
# after `prerender.mjs` has read it.
typescript/web/dist-ssr/
tmp/

# Local agent settings: machine-specific, never published.
.claude/

# Anything kept beside a file as a copy of it. `.env` is ignored by name, and a
# backup of it holds the same broker keys - this history opens whole, so a
# blanket `git add` must not be able to reach one. `*.bak` alone did not do it:
# on 27 August a copy named `.env.before-broker-fix` was left in the tree and was
# not ignored, so the pattern now covers every suffix and lets back the one file
# that is meant to be read.
*.bak
.env.*
!.env.example

transcripts/
# Stands in for the host's module cache when GOMODCACHE is unset, so the compose
# file renders from a bare .env.example instead of refusing to parse.
.gomodcache/
